# Everything the build context does not need. Without this file the whole
# repo is uploaded to the daemon on every build - including .venv (hundreds
# of MB) and .env (real credentials, which would then be readable in the
# image even though the COPY lines below never name it).

# Secrets. The container gets its configuration from the environment
# (--env-file, or the platform's variable settings), never from a baked-in
# file. Note that app/config.py's `env_file=".env"` simply finds nothing
# inside the image, which is the intended behaviour.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local Python environment and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Not part of the backend image
frontend/
stages/
tests/
docs/
.claude/
.github/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
!README.md

# Compose file describes the local Postgres dependency, not this image
docker-compose.yml
